A dead delivery worker's `review_deliveries` row is now finished as `landed` when its card is already `done`, and finished (done/abandoned) cards have their worktree, `ralph/*` branch, `worktrees` row and integrity baseline reclaimed by retention.

- `src/server/orchestrator.ts` — `reapStaleRuns()` no longer always fails a delivery whose claiming worker died mid-merge. When the card is already `done` or the run has an approved `reviews` row (i.e. `completeApproval` had landed the merge before the worker died) it calls the new private `finishLandedDelivery()` instead of `failDelivery()`: a CAS on `reviewDeliveries.status = running` to `finished` with `ok = 1`/`error = null`, one `review.decided` event tagged `recoveredAfterWorkerLoss`, and no card move — so two racing reapers still only let one through, and every other case keeps parking the card in Needs Attention.
- `src/server/retention.ts` — `removeAbandonedWorktrees()` became `removeFinishedWorktrees()`: it selects `removedAt IS NULL` rows for every card in `FINISHED_STATUSES` (done *and* abandoned) and now also deletes each run's integrity baseline via `removeBaseline(row.runId)` *before* `removeWorktree()`, because `removeWorktree` stamps `removedAt` and the sweep only re-selects unstamped rows — baseline-first keeps a failed pass retryable instead of stranding the baseline forever, matching `completeApproval` in `reviewService.ts`.
